     with ffoorrkk() and eexxeeccvvee(). Every further argument names a
     _f_i_l_e to bring up, in order.  A name ending in .ssll is a
     shared library: iinniitt starts it with ffoorrkk() and eexxeeccvvee(), and
     the child becomes the library's resident holder.  Any other
     name is a _d_r_i_v_e_r file, which iinniitt loads by running
     /eettcc/llooaadd. An empty argument, or a shared library whose file
     does not exist, is silently skipped; the system runs without
